AKESHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO SHIGEKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJII, MARI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOMURA, TAKESHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, SHIGEKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An unreduced dielectric ceramic material which is effective in avoiding the prolongation of a grinding step for exposing edges of nickel-containing internal electrodes in producing a layer-built ceramic capacitor having the electrodes, and which is obtained by adding MgO or a rare earth oxide to a calcine comprising as the main component a composite oxide represented by formula (I) [(CaXSr1-X)O]m[(TiYZr1-Y)O2] (wherein 0 &lt;/= X &lt;/= 1, 0 &lt;/= Y &lt;/= 0.10, and 0.75 &lt;/= m &lt;/= 1.04), in an amount of 0.001 to 10 mol.% based on the main component and then burning the calcine. The ceramic material contains SiO2, BaO and/or CaO, and MnO as minor ingredients in given amounts.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Matière céramique diélectrique non réduite qui est efficace pour éviter la prolongation d'une phase de meulage destinée à mettre à nu des arêtes d'électrodes internes contenant du nickel lors de la production d'un condensateur céramique à couches comportant lesdites électrodes. Ladite matière est obtenue par ajout de MgO ou d'un oxyde de terre rare à un calcinat contenant en tant que principal constituant un oxyde composite de formule [(CaXSr1-X)O]m[TiYZr1-Y)O2] (dans laquelle 0 &lt;/= X &lt;/= 1, 0 &lt;/= Y &lt;/= 0,10 et 0,75 &lt;/= m &lt;/= 1,04) à raison de 0,001 à 10 moles pour cent sur la base du constituant principal et puis à brûler le calcinat. Ladite matière céramique contient SiO2, BaO et/ou CaO et MnO en tant qu'ingrédients mineurs dans des quantités données.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>